    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0636" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.515 Gold Bloc/80: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-05-20T17:00:00+01:00">May 20, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 22—6:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. The Council today adopted the report of its <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >rapporteur</hi> on work of the Joint Committee on Clearing
                        Agreements<anchor n="10" xml:id="d418-f1"/> in which <pb facs="0637" n="535"
                        xml:id="pg535"/> governments are invited to consider the conclusions reached
                    by the Committee and as far as possible take account of them in regard to their
                    own countries and financial policy. The importance of the report was stressed by
                    the Australian and French delegates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d418-f1" n="10" xml:id="d418-f1-content">
                <p>For text of report, see League of Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Official
                        Journal</hi>, June 1935, p. 597.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
